{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## THE READ SIDE IS LIVE-PROVEN — run 30867072561, and the proof comes from an unexpected cell.\n\n`get_parent_map` reading the Epic Link is confirmed against a real DC instance, and the evidence is stronger than a dedicated cell would have given. `test_inbound_clear_parent_round_trips` reports:\n\n    the DC Epic Link was cleared (confirmed absent from BOTH the direct GET and the\n    SEARCH-BACKED PARENT MAP, WHICH 9bb9 TAUGHT TO READ IT)\n\nThat is this ticket's change doing its job on a live instance: the search-backed `get_parent_map` now tracks the Epic Link field, agrees with the direct GET, and does so through the shared `_resolve_epic_link_field_id()` discovery rather than a second parallel lookup.\n\nThe write side is proven in the same run — `test_outbound_epic_parent_round_trips_via_the_epic_link` executes and passes for the first time (see [rebar:3fe5-c22e-dc2d-4c9e]). So **the round trip closes end to end**: outbound writes the Epic Link, inbound reads it back.\n\n### AC status\n\n- [x] `get_parent_map` returns a non-sub-task's parent from the instance-discovered Epic Link\n- [x] the two shapes do not collide — the sub-task cells still exercise `fields.parent` and fail on the PLATFORM no-op ([rebar:1a9f-50c0-e7a5-4fda]), not on being rerouted to the Epic Link\n- [x] the round trip closes: a parent WRITTEN by outbound is SEEN by the next inbound read\n- [x] degradation contract preserved (unit-pinned; unchanged by this run)\n- [x] `transport.py` under the 800-LOC cap — comfortably: 465d split it to **230 lines** across five mixins, and `get_parent_map` now lives in `_hierarchy.py` (199)\n- [ ] idempotence: repeated passes over a converged epic-parent pair emit NO further mutation\n\n**Only idempotence is left, and I am not ticking it from this run.** The epic-parent cell passing proves ONE pass converges; it does not prove a SECOND pass is quiet. That is a distinct property and this epic has been burned four times by treating an adjacent green as evidence for a claim it does not make.\n\n### A REAL FINDING this cell surfaced, which is NOT this ticket's\n\nThe same cell then fails: the Epic Link is gone remotely, but `.parent_id` locally is still set. The remote clear works and the read sees it — the local side does not follow. Recorded on [rebar:37e7-d751-0042-4b94], which owns that cell."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785808274422930001,"uuid":"6b7f8210-90c6-46d5-9858-7dd6f869a1be"}